        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-17T03:27:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, but creating them here means the constructor must be running on the same thread where they\u0027re going to be used because the contents are `byte[]` which are necessarily mutable. That means the constructor would need to run on the same thread as the reading code, which is not the case today.\n\nSo the current patchset creates the messages on demand and always on the correct thread, which is still easy to understand, but doesn\u0027t have the issue.",
      "parentUuid": "2ff53ee2_87d5d22d",
